(ABSTRACT:) Tj
0 -15 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Hao Ngashan embodies the unwritten constitutional and customary legal) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(code governing Tangkhul society since time immemorial. This paper) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(analyzes the structural pillars of Tangkhul customary jurisprudence: the) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(patrilineal clan system \(Shang\), strict clan exogamy \(Kashan\), land) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(tenure mechanisms, the judicial authority of the Village Council) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(\(Hangva\), and traditional dispute settlement procedures. We examine the) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(sacred oath-taking formula \(Tuishot\) and demonstrate how customary law) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(operates harmoniously alongside modern constitutional protections in) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Manipur.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Keywords: Hao Ngashan, Customary Law, Clan Exogamy, Hangva, Shimxang, Tuishot, Jurisprudence) Tj
0 -14 Td
