(1. THE CLAN \(SHANG\) AND EXOGAMOUS MARRIAGE \(KASHAN\)) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Tangkhul social structure is organized into patrilineal clans \(Shang\)) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(that trace their descent from common ancestors. The bedrock principle of) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(social ethics is Kashan--strict clan exogamy. Intermarriage within the) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(same Shang is considered an intolerable moral taboo \(Kashansha\) that) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(historically incurred banishment from the village territory. All) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(marriages must link distinct Shangs, creating enduring reciprocal) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(obligations and alliances across the community.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
